{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he is a leper or a zav.</b> It says: not only this but even that. Not only a leper, but even a zav is forbidden; and not only a zav, whose impurity emerges from his body, but even one defiled by a corpse is forbidden; and not only one defiled by a corpse, who is impure with seven-day impurity, but even a ba'al keri, who is impure only with evening impurity, is forbidden; and not only a ba'al keri, whose impurity is from his body, but even one impure through contact-impurity is forbidden." "<b>Until he is purified.</b> Just as the purification mentioned below requires sunset, so too here it requires sunset."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:12.915688810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}